            "sources": {
                "pole": "Poled standing, as the dugout her hull is: her float makes her far stiffer than the narrowest canoe polers stand in (bin/lib/hulls/physics.py). Outrigger canoes are poled in shallows (NOAA, Ponape 1971), but no source says where the poler stands, so he stands where the dugout's does, at the end her rower faces. His hands end the shove at his hip (0.530 of a 1.756 m stature: Drillis & Contini 1966; ANSUR II, Gordon et al. 2014); his eyes at vanilla's standing 1.7 m",
                "sideDrag": "A round-bottomed log: the round-bilged hull's cross-flow drag"
            }
        },
