            "damage": {"material": "wood"},
            "sources": {
                "parts": "By the model (bin/lib/hulls/outrigger.py), in oak: her hull is the dugout she was built on; her float, a log hewn round with pointed ends; her poles (three crooked booms 9 cm across, a mast 9 cm across, two spars 7.5 cm); her washstrakes, boards 2.5 cm thick, as they are fitted. A float or poles of another wood weigh by their own",
                "impactCapacity": "The dugout's hull, in her hull's wood alone: the float and rig lashed to it take no knock a hull takes",
                "shell": "The dugout's walls, about 5 cm thick, as the Dufuna canoe's (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dufuna_canoe)",
                "repairs": "Her hull is a dugout's, mended as one"
            },
            "hullBoxMetres": {"from": [-2.5, 0, -0.45], "to": [2.5, 0.565, 0.45]},
            "hullBoxVoxels": {"from": [-40, 0, -7.2], "to": [40, 9.044, 7.2]}
        },
